<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · 1848 · Europe</p><h1 class="sg-title">Maamme</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="sv">Maamme</bdi> / <bdi lang="sv-Latn">Vårt land</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>The anthem of Finland: a Swedish poem by Johan Ludvig Runeberg, set to music by Fredrik Pacius and first sung on 13 May 1848.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Johan Ludvig Runeberg (Swedish); Julius Krohn (Finnish translation)</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>Fredrik Pacius</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Finns, Swedish- and Finnish-speaking; the Finnish state</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swedish, Finnish</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Finland</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>poem written 1846, printed 1848; first performed 13 May 1848</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (Swedish words by Johan Ludvig Runeberg (written 1846, printed 1848); music by Fredrik Pacius (1848); Finnish text by Julius Krohn (1867))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maamme">Maamme</a>&quot; (&quot;Our Land&quot;), known by its original Swedish title as &quot;Vårt land&quot;, is the de facto national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. Its words are the prologue to Johan Ludvig Runeberg's verse cycle The Tales of Ensign Stål (Fänrik Ståhls sägner), a classic example of Romantic nationalism. The poem, written in Swedish in 1846 but not printed until 1848, has eleven stanzas. The music was composed by the German immigrant Fredrik Pacius, who is said to have written the tune in four days, and the song was first performed on 13 May 1848.</p><p>The Finnish text sung today is usually credited to Paavo Cajander's 1889 translation of Ensign Stål, but it in fact comes from the 1867 translation by Julius Krohn. In the 1880s and again in the 1920s there were attempts to replace the song with one written in Finnish, but these ceased by the 1930s. The song was popular throughout the 19th century, yet it gained its present position only after Pacius's death. Its melody is also used for the Estonian anthem &quot;Mu isamaa, mu õnn ja rõõm&quot; (&quot;My Fatherland, My Happiness and Joy&quot;) and for the Livonian anthem &quot;Min izāmō&quot; (&quot;My Fatherland&quot;).</p><p>No law makes &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maamme">Maamme</a>&quot; the anthem, in the way that laws define <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>'s coat of arms and flag; its place has been established by convention, and in 2018 the Government of Finland described it as the &quot;Finnish national anthem&quot;. Its status is still debated from time to time. Some <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finns">Finns</a> would prefer &quot;Finlandia&quot; by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-sibelius">Jean Sibelius</a>, with words by V. A. Koskenniemi in Finnish and Joel Rundt in Swedish: opposing legislative initiatives in the Finnish Parliament in 2003 proposed making either &quot;Maamme&quot; or the Finlandia Hymn the official anthem, a citizens' initiative of 2014 asked for the Finlandia Hymn, and in 2016 members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-coalition-party">National Coalition Party</a> campaigned for it, but opinion in the party was divided and the campaign fell short.</p><p>In practice &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maamme">Maamme</a>&quot; serves as the national anthem: it is played during state visits and represents <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> at international sporting events. Usually only the first and the last verses are sung. When Finnish and Swedish speakers are gathered together, three verses are sung: the first in Finnish, the first in Swedish and the last in Finnish.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A hymn of love for the homeland: the singers declare that no land, however rich or fair, is dearer to them than their own poor northern country, honour its forebears' struggles, and end in the hope that its future will one day flower. The mood is earnest and tender.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">Swedish</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-2"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Swedish</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vårt land, vårt land, vårt fosterland,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our land, our land, our Fatherland!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ljud högt, o dyra ord!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ring out, dear word, oh sound!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ej lyfts en höjd mot himlens rand,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>No rising hill, or mountain grand,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ej sänks en dal, ej sköljs en strand,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>No sloping dale, no northern strand,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Mer älskad än vår bygd i nord,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>There is, more loved, to be found,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Än våra fäders jord.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Than this — our fathers’ ground.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vårt land är fattigt, skall så bli</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our land is poor, and so shall be</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">För den, som guld begär,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To him who gold will crave.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">En främling far oss stolt förbi;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The strangers proudly pass, but we</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Men detta landet älska vi,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Shall ever love this land, we see,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">För oss med moar, fjäll och skär</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In moor, and fell, and isle and wave,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ett guldland dock det är.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>A golden land, so brave.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vi älska våra strömmars brus</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>We love our rippling brooks, so bright,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och våra bäckars språng,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our gushing streams, so strong,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Den mörka skogens dystra sus,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The whisper of dark woods, at night,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vår stjärnenatt, vårt sommarljus,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our starry skies, our summer light,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Allt, allt, vad här som syn, som sång</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>All, all that we, in sight and song,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vårt hjärta rört en gång.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Have felt and lived among.</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 66 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Här striddes våra fäders strid</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Here fought our fathers, without fear,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Med tanke, svärd och plog,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>With sword, and plough, and thought.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Här, här, i klar som mulen tid,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And here, in clouded times, and clear,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Med lycka hård, med lycka blid,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>With fortune in their front or rear,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Det finska folkets hjärta slog,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Their Finnish hearts have beat, and wrought</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Här bars, vad det fördrog.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And borne what bear they ought.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vem täljde väl de striders tal,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who tells, of all the fights, the tale,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Som detta folk bestod,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In which this folk withstood,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Då kriget röt från dal till dal,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>When war did rage from dale to dale,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Då frosten kom med hungerns kval,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>When frost set in, with hunger’s wail?</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vem mätte allt dess spillda blod</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who measured all their pouring blood,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och allt dess tålamod?</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And all their patience good?</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och det var här, det blodet flöt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And it was here their blood was shed,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ja, här för oss det var,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>For us, here, on this shore;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och det var här, sin fröjd det njöt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And it was here their joys were bred,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och det var här, sin suck det göt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Here, that their sighs were heaved and fled,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Det folk, som våra bördor bar</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>That people’s who our burdens bore</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Långt före våra dar.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Before us, long before.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Här är oss ljuvt, här är oss gott,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Here it is sweet and good, we wot,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Här är oss allt beskärt;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>All, too, is giv’n us here;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Hur ödet kastar än vår lott,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>However fate may cast our lot,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ett land, ett fosterland vi fått,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>A land, a fatherland, we’ve got.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vad finns på jorden mera värt</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Will there a thing on earth appear</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Att hållas dyrt och kärt?</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>More worthy, to hold dear?</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och här och här är detta land,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And here’s, and here’s this fatherland,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">vårt öga ser det här;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Here every eye it sees;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vi kunna sträcka ut vår hand</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And we can stretch a pointing hand,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och visa glatt på sjö och strand</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To show, with joy, its sea and strand,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och säga: se det landet där,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And say, “Behold this country, this,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vårt fosterland det är!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our Fatherland it is.”</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och fördes vi att bo i glans</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And if we once were made to rise</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Bland guldmoln i det blå,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To gold clouds, from below,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och blev vårt liv en stjärnedans,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And if we moved in starry skies,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Där tår ej göts, där suck ej fanns,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Where no one weeps, where no one sighs,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Till detta arma land ändå</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To this poor lonely country, though,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vår längtan skulle stå.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our longing hearts would go.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">O land, du tusen sjöars land,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Oh land, the thousand lakes’ own land,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Där sång och trohet byggt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Of faith, and lay, and glee,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Där livets hav oss gett en strand,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Where life’s main sea gave us a strand,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vår forntids land, vår framtids land,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our fore-time’s land, our future’s land,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Var för din fattigdom ej skyggt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Shy of thy poorness, never be,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Var fritt, var glatt, var tryggt!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Be calm, be glad, be free!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Din blomning, sluten än i knopp,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thy blossom, hidden now from sight,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Skall mogna ur sitt tvång;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Shall burst its bud ere long.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Se, ur vår kärlek skall gå opp</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Lo! from our love, shall rise aright,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Ditt ljus, din glans, din fröjd, ditt hopp,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thy sun, thy hope, thy joy, thy light,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Och högre klinga skall en gång</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And higher, once, more full and strong,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sv">Vår fosterländska sång.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Shall ring Our Country’s song.</span></p></div></details></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Johan Ludvig Runeberg, Fänrik Ståls sägner (1848). Text from <a href="https://sv.wikisource.org/wiki/V%C3%A5rt_land" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p><p>English: tr. Anna Krook (1904). Text from <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Our_Land_(Krook)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p></div></section>
